# Requests to try with VS Code's REST Client extension.
# Start the server first (npm start), then click Send Request above any request.
# The answers below are for the center's 12 pets: load them into maple_street first (the README shows how).

### The first page: 5 pets in name order, Bean to Juniper: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/pets

### The third page: Rocket and Ziggy: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/pets?page=3

### The cats that are good with kids: Juniper, Olive and Pickles: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/pets?species=cat&goodWithKids=true

### Mochi: 200
GET http://localhost:3100/pets/6740c0000000000000000002

### No pet has this id: 404
GET http://localhost:3100/pets/6740c0000000000000000099

### "2" isn't a pet id: 400
GET http://localhost:3100/pets/2

### Add Waffles: 201, Waffles with a new id and the status "available"
POST http://localhost:3100/pets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Waffles", "species": "dog", "age": 4, "traits": ["good with kids"] }

### Another pet named Biscuit: 409
POST http://localhost:3100/pets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Biscuit", "species": "dog", "age": 5, "traits": ["calm"] }

### Rocket is adopted: 200, Rocket with the status "adopted"
PATCH http://localhost:3100/pets/6740c0000000000000000006
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "adopted" }
